---
title: "get_daily_attendance_details (Attendance Summary Functions)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: receive(for_date)
    q_init --> q_cte: CTE daily_attendees
    q_cte --> q_filter_date: date = for_date AND type = 'in'
    q_filter_date --> q_distinct: SELECT DISTINCT user_id
    q_distinct --> q_join_members: JOIN member.members m ON supabase_auth_user_id = user_id
    q_join_members --> q_check_deleted: check m.deleted_at IS NULL
    q_check_deleted --> q_join_team: deleted_at IS NULL (include)
    q_check_deleted --> q_skip: deleted_at IS NOT NULL (exclude)
    q_skip --> q_join_members: next row
    q_join_team --> q_left_join_rel: LEFT JOIN member.member_team_relations mtr
    q_left_join_rel --> q_left_join_teams: LEFT JOIN member.teams t ON mtr.team_id = t.id
    q_left_join_teams --> q_coalesce: COALESCE(t.name, '未所属')
    q_coalesce --> q_group: GROUP BY t.name, m.generation
    q_group --> q_count: COUNT(m.supabase_auth_user_id)
    q_count --> [*]: ORDER BY team_name, generation, return rows

    note right of q_filter_date
        INV-001: Only attendance records for the exact for_date with type 'in' are selected
        INV-002: Each user_id appears at most once in daily_attendees (DISTINCT)
    end note

    note right of q_check_deleted
        INV-003: Soft-deleted members (deleted_at IS NOT NULL) are excluded from results
    end note

    note right of q_coalesce
        INV-004: Members without team assignment get team_name = '未所属' (unaffiliated)
        INV-005: LEFT JOINs ensure members without team relations are still included
    end note

    note right of q_group
        INV-006: Results are grouped by (team_name, generation) with count of members per group
        INV-007: Result is ordered by team_name then generation ascending
    end note
